  "question": {
    "text": "A cylinder of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is released from rest from the top of an inclined plane of inclination <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the cylinder rolls without slipping, then its speed when it reaches the bottom&nbsp;is [<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"
